WEBVTT

00:00:01.682 --> 00:00:05.435
- Good afternoon, class.
- Good afternoon, madam hooch.

00:00:05.644 --> 00:00:08.438
Good afternoon, Amanda.
Good afternoon.

00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:12.192
Welcome to your first flying lesson.

00:00:12.401 --> 00:00:16.321
What are you waiting for?
Step up to your broomstick.

00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:22.119
Come on now, hurry up. Stick your hand
over the broom and say, "up."

00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:32.129
Up. Up!

00:00:32.337 --> 00:00:34.339
With feeling.

00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:35.591
All: Up!

00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:42.097
Up! Om

00:00:43.015 --> 00:00:45.142
shut up, Harry.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.022
Now, once you've got hold of
your broom, I want you to mount it.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:54.234
Grip it tight. You don't wanna be
sliding off the end.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:59.531
When I blow my whistle, I want you
to kick off from the ground, hard.

00:00:59.781 --> 00:01:03.619
Keep your broom steady,
hover for a moment...

00:01:03.827 --> 00:01:08.123
Then lean fonnard slightly
and touch back down.

00:01:08.373 --> 00:01:11.501
On my whistle. Three, two...

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:15.297
Mr. Longbottom.

00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:22.804
- Mr. Longbottom!
- Down, down!

00:01:23.013 --> 00:01:24.264
Neville!

00:01:27.976 --> 00:01:30.646
Come back down this instant!

00:01:40.572 --> 00:01:43.075
Mr. Longbo...

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.503
Neville: Whoa!

00:01:59.591 --> 00:02:02.010
Madam hooch:
Everyone out of the way!

00:02:07.557 --> 00:02:09.726
Is he all right?

00:02:10.102 --> 00:02:15.774
Oh, dear, it's a broken wrist.
Poor boy. Come on now, up you get.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:21.738
Keep your feet on the ground
while I take him to the hospital wing.

00:02:21.947 --> 00:02:25.617
Understand? If I see
a single broom in the air...

00:02:25.826 --> 00:02:31.081
The one riding it will be expelled
before they can say ouidditch.

00:02:31.289 --> 00:02:33.208
Did you see his face?

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:37.254
If he had squeezed this, he'd have
remembered to fall on his arse.

00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:39.965
Give it here, Malfoy.

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:44.469
No. I'll leave it somewhere
for Longbottom to find.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.143
How about on the roof?

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:56.148
What's the matter, Potter?
Bit beyond your reach?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:02.487
Harry, no way!
You heard what madam hooch said.

00:03:02.654 --> 00:03:05.615
Besides, you don't know how to fly.

00:03:11.163 --> 00:03:14.666
Give it here or I'll
knock you off your broom!

00:03:14.916 --> 00:03:17.002
Is that so?

00:03:20.172 --> 00:03:22.466
Have it your way, then.

00:03:55.207 --> 00:03:58.835
Boy 1: Nice going, Harry.
Boy 2: That was wicked, Harry!

00:03:59.044 --> 00:04:01.046
Harry Potter!

00:04:02.047 --> 00:04:04.049
Follow me.

00:04:15.727 --> 00:04:17.979
You wait here.

00:04:19.731 --> 00:04:25.028
Professor quirrell, excuse me.
Could I borrow wood for a moment?

00:04:25.237 --> 00:04:27.072
Yes, of course.

00:04:32.744 --> 00:04:38.500
Potter, this is Oliver wood.
Wood, I have found you a seeker.

00:04:40.585 --> 00:04:44.089
Have you heard? Harry Potter's
the new Gryffindor seeker.

00:04:44.339 --> 00:04:46.550
I always knew he'd do well.

00:04:47.008 --> 00:04:51.054
Seeker? But first years
never make the house teams.

00:04:51.263 --> 00:04:56.101
- You must be the youngest player in...
- A century, McGonagall says.

00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:58.603
Well done, Harry.
Wood's just told us.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.273
Fred and George are on the team.
Beaters.

00:05:01.523 --> 00:05:05.235
Our job is to make sure you
don't get bloodied up too bad.

00:05:05.443 --> 00:05:08.113
Can't make any promises.
Rough game, Quidditch.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.284
But no one's died in years.
Someone vanishes occasionally.

00:05:12.492 --> 00:05:15.245
But they'll turn up in a month or two.

00:05:15.495 --> 00:05:21.126
Go on. Quidditch is great. Best game
there is, and you'll be great too.

00:05:21.293 --> 00:05:24.546
I've never played.
What if I make a fool of myself?

00:05:24.963 --> 00:05:29.759
You won't make a fool of yourself.
It's in your blood.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.147
You never told me your father
was a seeker too.

